_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 10
---
order: 10
---
short_label: VII.10
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If a number is a parts of a number, and another is the same parts of another, then alternately, whatever part of parts the first is of the third, the same part, or the same parts, the second is of the fourth.
----
proof:

Let the number {AB} be parts of the number {C}, and another number {DE} be the same parts of another number {F}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="150" height="270" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VII.10 diagram" src="propVII10.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // AB is two thirds of C and DE two thirds of F; AG, GB and DH, HE are
    // the parts. Line segments only, so the walk is highlight beats, with
    // G and H appearing when AB and DE are divided.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","AB","C","D","E","DE","F"];
    var DIV1  = GIVEN.concat(["G","AG","GB"]);
    var DIV2  = DIV1.concat(["H","DH","HE"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
